  "title": "Razia Sultana, ruler of the Delhi Sultanate",
  "summary": "Razia Sultana ruled the Delhi Sultanate from 1236 to 1240 and is described as its first and only woman ruler. Her father Iltutmish named her heir, but nobles installed her brother first; she took the throne in November 1236. Turkish nobles resented her, and she was defeated by her brother Bahram Shah in October 1240.",
